/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (RPM or .rpm \(Red Hat based softwares.\)  It is a package management system. The name RPM variously refers to the .rpm file format, files in this format, software packaged in such files, and the package manager itself. RPM was intended primarily for Linux distributions; the file format is the baseline package format of the Linux Standard Base. RPM was developed by Community & Red Hat.  Example: Google chrome software  Package Name: google-chrome-stable-57.0.2987.133-1.x86_64.rpm  Installation: rpm -ivh google-chrome-stable-57.0.2987.133-1.x86_64.rpm )
/E (RPM or .rpm \(Red Hat based softwares.\)  It is a package management system. The name RPM variously refers to the .rpm file format, files in this format, software packaged in such files, and the package manager itself. RPM was intended primarily for Linux distributions; the file format is the baseline package format of the Linux Standard Base. RPM was developed by Community & Red Hat.  Example: Google chrome software  Package Name: google-chrome-stable-57.0.2987.133-1.x86_64.rpm  Installation: rpm -ivh google-chrome-stable-57.0.2987.133-1.x86_64.rpm )
/Pg 11 0 R
